	"exhibition_history_text": "M.H. DeYoung Memorial Museum: The Childhood of Christ, 1967;\r\nUniversity Art Museum, University of California, Berkeley:  Master Drawings from California Collections, 1968, cat. no. 41, p. 47, repr.p. 122, in which Keith Thoreen , under supervision of Professor Juergen Schulz, discusses Maturino and Polidoro and accepts the attribution to Maturino.;\r\nUtah Museum of Fine Arts: Aspects of the Italian Renaissance, 1973.",
	"bibliography_text": null,
	"provenance": "Provenance: Joseph Green Cogswell; Mortimer Leo Schiff; Moore S. Achenbach;\r\nCogswell no. 170 , Hellman no. 96  as “ An Angel” by Maturino da Firenze (George S. Hellman, Original Drawings by the Old Masters: The Collection formed by Joseph Green Cogswell, 1786-1871, New York: privately published, 1915);\r\nNotes from old file:\r\nPhyllis Hattis suggested possible 17th century artist and Agnes Mongan (A.M. July 1972) agreed;\r\nNote:  previously unknown verso of drawing uncovered by removal of old mount  in conservation by WRPCL in February 1991, and now matted separately (1963.24.19v)",
